    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "An exceptional meteorological event, verified by records as one of the heaviest rainy seasons in three decades, triggered a flood causation sequence. Reservoirs filled beyond 97% capacity, and dam operations combined with seasonal rains pushed the Euphrates past protective embankments, leading to a structural failure confirmed on-site as an earthen bridge collapsed. The naval contingent then deployed boats for evacuations, while the head of state assessed the damage in the Syrian regions.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "how-4"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [
        "how_fragments_expanded_to_contiguous_span"
      ],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The confirmed fatalities among children, a tragic disaster outcome, resulted from the verified extent of the inundation that flooded homes, farms, and schools. This disaster impact prompted the observed rescue operation by the maritime evacuation force and led to a formalized commitment to limit water flow, a diplomatic agreement to limit discharges reached with the upstream dam operator.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "result-0",
          "result-1",
          "result-3",
          "result-4"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.78
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The documented sequence of cause and effect, from the heavy rainfall to the resulting flooding damage, was traced through the primary climatic cause. The executive's on-site assessment followed the bridge failure and the publicized use of naval resources, highlighting the international cooperation in flood mitigation measures.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
